                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Like many others before me, I played this game a decade ago when it came out. And like many others since, I got bored very quickly and stopped playing. I recently started it again because I've been trying to achievement farm all these small titles I have collected over the years. Why you ask? I dunno. But this game was brutal to say the least. Half of the items don't even work. Basically the only things that do work are the extra damage items to the monsters with whatever hashtag vulnerability they have. Any passive item that is supposed to increase the players stats or give health steal or gold steal or whatever doesn't work. Any item that gives passive bonuses to your fellow (thats what they call tamed pets in this game) don't work. The active items are about 50/50 when it comes to working. For instance, the active that consumes a key and gives you 250 exp, that one works. The active that gives you bonus XP with every click for 30 seconds, that one doesn't work. Same for the HP life steal one, doesn't work. It makes the game more challenging than it needed to be. All I can say is, a good strat that I used was to farm keys, and use the item that converts them to EXP, and then use that to level up fast. Also farm for those darn tickets that make your gear upgrades cheaper. Save them for when you get to the 10th level upgrade because the price increase is stupid ridiculous. Also something that kind of works is the pokeball thing that allows you to catch the rare fellows that require diamonds to purchase, A currency that you can't get anymore because I guess diamonds were tied to events or purchasing with money, both of which are discontinued. I had 3 diamonds when I started back up, pretty sure that's just pitty diamonds that every new game get's. I used them to get an extra slot in my inventory because I felt it was worth it. But yea use the pokeballs to catch one of the higher level fellows that have their own inventory slots. I managed to finally get a mermaid, but I used well over 35 dang balls on the stupid hippogryph thing with no luck. Only took 6 tries with the mermaid, which has 4 extra slots. But yea get something like that for the extra inventory slots. Level it up if you want, or don't. It doesn't really matter because most of your damage is done with your click attacks, and you should be using an auto clicker. I went 20 DMG (click damage), then 20 DEF (health points), then got up to 100 DMG, and then went for 200 Luck (luck is Luck% [assuming for gold drops and maybe catching fellows?] and Crit Chance), which on the hardest difficulty gave me like 70% crit chance, which is double damage. So I was hitting at the end 2.4k without any bonus damage from the item buffs targeting vulnerabilities.\n\nTLDR: This game is boring, unless you want to spend like 10+ hours for the achievements, then move on to something else.",
